{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## RCA — RE-POSTED (the original write was stranded by this very bug)\n\nA `/rebar-debug` investigation on 2026-08-28 proved the root cause and posted it here. That\ncomment never reached the shared store — this ticket showed **zero comments**. The analysis of\nthe stranded-writes bug was itself stranded. Re-recording it durably.\n\n## Root cause: STARVATION, not a wedged store\n\nRecovery works; the store is healthy. `origin/tickets` was receiving a push every **2-4s\n(median 3s)** from the enrichment pipeline, while one fetch->merge->push recovery cycle costs\n**>= 2.4s, rising to >= 4.2s** as `_cas_backoff` escalates. The quiet window a recovering writer\nneeds is >= the interval between competing pushes, so the race is *structurally* unwinnable.\n\n### Decisive evidence\n\n**1. Recovery runs; every merge succeeds.** The container's reflog showed `fetch ...\nfast-forward` every 3-6s, each followed by a clean `ort` merge. No lock timeouts. Rules out\n\"recovery never runs\".\n\n**2. 84% of the backlog was recovery's OWN merge commits:**\n\n    150  merge commits (\"Merge origin/tickets (auto-reconcile during push retry)\")\n     28  real ticket events\n\n150/28 = **5.4 merges per event** = `_MAX_RETRIES = 5` (`src/rebar/_store/push_classify.py:62`)\nplus the terminal push. **Every write exhausted its budget and lost.** Oldest local-only commit\nwas ~4h old, ~168 consecutive attempts, zero successes.\n\nThis inverts the naive reading: monotone growth is the PREDICTED signature of persistent\nrace-loss, because recovery inflates the backlog it is draining by ~6 commits per failed write.\nMeasured 178 -> 196 in 61s.\n\n**3. Why it cannot be won** (timed read-only in-container): `git ls-remote` 509ms (network RTT\nfloor) + `git status` 885ms (27.5 MB index, 169,843 files) + `git push --dry-run` 742ms +\n`_cas_backoff` 250/500/1000/2000ms = a **2.4-4.2s** window against a 2-4s competing-push\ninterval.\n\n**4. Load-regime change.** `origin/tickets` went from ~20-90 commits/hour to **~1000-1400 at\n2026-08-27 21:00 UTC**. Driver: the enrichment queue auto-pushed a separate commit per queue\ntransition (ENQUEUE -> CLAIM -> DIGEST -> DONE, ~4 pushed commits/ticket,\n`src/rebar/llm/overlap/queue.py:99,107`), sweeping 491 distinct tickets in 3h.\n\n**5. Winner-takes-all.** After a success your ref IS origin's tip, so the next push is a bare\nfast-forward (~0.7s, no fetch, no merge). Fall behind ONCE and you pay the 2.4-4.2s merge window\nforever.\n\n**6. `_cas_backoff` is inverted for this failure mode.** `src/rebar/_store/push_recovery.py:405-410`\nsleeps AFTER the merge and BEFORE the push with **no re-fetch between**, on an unjittered\nschedule — so each retry is strictly staler than the last and all starved writers retry in\nlockstep.\n\n### Rivals ruled out\n\n- **Stale build** — REJECTED (`git merge-base --is-ancestor 7be0edb7132d 6fe5c0d54574` -> true).\n- **Credential asymmetry** — REJECTED: `push --dry-run` authenticates and reaches a ref-level\n  `! [rejected] ... (fetch first)`; a permission failure would be 403/denied.\n- **Not genuinely non-fast-forward** — REJECTED: `ls-remote` returned a sha `cat-file -e` could\n  not resolve locally.\n- **Container-specific** — REJECTED, the strongest discriminator: the developer-side store showed\n  the identical failure concurrently (397 ahead, 306 of them merges).\n\n## Mitigation applied 2026-08-28 and its measured effect\n\nOperator-directed: the opportunistic write-path enrichment drain was turned OFF via\n`overlap_drain = \"off\"` in the `[llm]` table. (Note `[tool.rebar.llm]` is NOT parsed — a\ndocumentation defect fixed separately in `eyeable-intimate-marmoset`.) Effect: the local store\nwent from **619 unpushed to ahead=0 behind=0**. Contention fell far enough that pushes win.\n\n## AC2 CONTRADICTS A STANDING OPERATOR DECISION\n\nAC2 requires a write that cannot reach the shared store to \"FAIL LOUDLY to the caller rather\nthan returning success\". That is the opposite of **operator decision B4**, recorded on closed bug\n`e1ed-b700-c442-4d0c` (`vapoury-attack-lamb`) under \"## Approved remedy (operator decision B4)\":\n\n> \"The remedy must be a SIGNAL, never an exception or a non-zero exit.\"\n> \"OUT of scope: changing CLI behaviour or any exit code, raising on the default path ...\"\n\nPinned in `docs/concurrency.md:551,594` and `src/rebar/_store/push_classify.py:40`. B4's remedy\nalready SHIPPED and works: every MCP write returns `push_status: final-push-rejected`. The honest\nreframing is **\"the signal is present and being ignored\"**, not \"the signal is missing\".\n\n**AC2 should be rewritten, not implemented.** Escalated to the operator."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787952416712122688,"uuid":"97e23f72-945b-402d-aada-41c8c068e309"}